      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The shame is a heavy cloak, but it's also a heavy anchor, and you don't have to carry it anymore. Stopping the fight isn't giving up; it's finally choosing peace over the constant, draining performance of 'being okay.' Imagine the quiet that comes when you stop trying to prove your worth to people who were only ever interested in the idea of you. That quiet is a real, attainable place.",
